// `std.list`: the home of the native finite lists. `List(A)` is the list type
// over a value type `A`, its values `nil`, `cons` and the literal `[a, b]`. A
// source names it by listing it, `import std.list (List);`.
//
// The former is native, so no declaration here states it. The lowering
// answers `List` in a source that lists it from this module, and nowhere
// else. The everyday functions and their laws wait for demand.
//
// - see: #4520
